Subject: Spell xgetbv as an instruction rather than raw bytes
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

Fil-C recognizes and safely lowers xgetbv with these register constraints.
The older raw-byte encoding hides the instruction from that analysis.
Keep CPU feature detection and SIMD dispatch enabled.

--- a/spa/plugins/support/cpu-x86.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/support/cpu-x86.c
@@ -114,7 +114,7 @@
 	(XSTATE_SSE | XSTATE_YMM | XSTATE_OPMASK | XSTATE_ZMM | XSTATE_HI_ZMM)
 
 	if (has_osxsave)
-		asm (".byte 0x0f; .byte 0x01; .byte 0xd0"
+		asm ("xgetbv"
 			: "=a" (eax), "=d" (edx)
 			: "c" (XCR_XFEATURE_ENABLED_MASK));
 	else
